### Description

This Terraform configuration creates an IAM role named 'eks-cluster-1' with an assume role policy allowing the 'eks.amazonaws.com' service to assume the role. It attaches the 'AmazonEKSClusterPolicy' IAM policy to this role. Additionally, it defines an AWS EKS cluster named based on the provided cluster name variable and version, associating it with the IAM role. The cluster's VPC is configured with subnet IDs for networking, including private and public subnets in the specified AWS region.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "cluster_name" {
  description = "Name of the EKS cluster"
  default     = "my-eks-cluster"
}

variable "cluster_version" {
  description = "Version of the EKS cluster"
  default     = "1.24"
}

variable "subnet_ids" {
  description = "List of subnet IDs for the EKS cluster VPC"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]  # Replace with actual subnet IDs
}

# Create IAM role for EKS cluster
resource "aws_iam_role" "eks_cluster_1_role" {
  name = "eks-cluster-1"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "eks.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

# Attach AmazonEKSClusterPolicy to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach_amazon_eks_cluster_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSClusterPolicy"
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_1_role.name
}

# Create EKS cluster
resource "aws_eks_cluster" "eks_cluster" {
  name     = var.cluster_name
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_1_role.arn
  version  = var.cluster_version

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids = var.subnet_ids
  }

  # Ensure that IAM Role permissions are created before and deleted
  # after EKS Cluster handling. Otherwise, EKS will not be able to
  # properly delete EKS managed EC2 infrastructure such as Security Groups.
  depends_on = [
    aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.attach_amazon_eks_cluster_policy,
  ]
}
```

### Notes

- **Region**: The AWS provider is configured to use the 'us-west-2' region. You can change this to your desired region.
- **Cluster Name and Version**: The cluster name and version are provided as variables with default values. You can override these values when applying the Terraform configuration.
- **Subnet IDs**: The subnet IDs are provided as a variable. You must replace the default subnet IDs with actual subnet IDs from your AWS account.
- **IAM Role and Policy**: The IAM role 'eks-cluster-1' is created with an assume role policy allowing 'eks.amazonaws.com' to assume the role. The 'AmazonEKSClusterPolicy' is attached to this role.
- **EKS Cluster**: The EKS cluster is created with the specified name, version, and VPC configuration using the provided subnet IDs. The cluster depends on the IAM role policy attachment to ensure proper setup.

