### Description
The Terraform program below creates an AWS EKS cluster named "example" and adds the "vpc-cni" addon to it. The program includes the necessary resources and configurations to ensure the EKS cluster and addon are properly set up.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "eks_cluster_role" {
  name = "eks-cluster-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "eks.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "eks_cluster_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSClusterPolicy"
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_role.name
}

resource "aws_vpc" "example_vpc" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
  tags = {
    Name = "example-vpc"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "example_subnet" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.example_vpc.id
  cidr_block        = "10.0.1.0/24"
  availability_zone = "us-west-2a"
  tags = {
    Name = "example-subnet"
  }
}

resource "aws_eks_cluster" "example_cluster" {
  name     = "example"
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_role.arn

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids = [aws_subnet.example_subnet.id]
  }

  depends_on = [
    aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.eks_cluster_policy,
  ]
}

resource "aws_eks_addon" "example_vpc_cni_addon" {
  cluster_name = aws_eks_cluster.example_cluster.name
  addon_name   = "vpc-cni"

  depends_on = [
    aws_eks_cluster.example_cluster,
  ]
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the "us-west-2" region.
2. **IAM Role for EKS Cluster**: An IAM role named "eks-cluster-role" is created with the necessary trust policy to allow EKS to assume the role.
3. **IAM Role Policy Attachment**: The "AmazonEKSClusterPolicy" policy is attached to the IAM role.
4. **VPC and Subnet**: A VPC and a subnet are created to provide networking for the EKS cluster.
5. **EKS Cluster**: An EKS cluster named "example" is created with the specified IAM role and VPC configuration.
6. **EKS Addon**: The "vpc-cni" addon is added to the EKS cluster, ensuring it depends on the cluster being created first.

