### Description
This Terraform configuration sets up two AWS S3 buckets with specific access control and logging features. The first bucket is set to private, while the second bucket is configured to allow log delivery writes. Additionally, logging for the private bucket is enabled, sending logs to the second bucket with a specified log file prefix.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify the desired AWS region
}

# Define the first S3 bucket with private access control
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "private_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-private-bucket"
  acl    = "private"
}

# Define the second S3 bucket to store logs
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "log_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-log-bucket"
  acl    = "log-delivery-write"
}

# Configure logging for the private bucket to send logs to the log bucket
resource "aws_s3_bucket_logging" "bucket_logging" {
  bucket      = aws_s3_bucket.private_bucket.id
  target_bucket = aws_s3_bucket.log_bucket.id
  target_prefix = "log/"
}
```

This configuration ensures that the private bucket is accessible only to the owner, while the log bucket is configured to accept logs from the private bucket. The logging configuration specifies that logs should be stored in the log bucket with the prefix "log/".

