### Description
This Terraform configuration creates an AWS S3 bucket with a specified name and sets its ownership controls to ensure that the bucket owner automatically owns and has full control over every object in the bucket. The configuration includes the creation of the S3 bucket and the subsequent setup of ownership controls referencing the bucket's ID.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify the desired AWS region
}

# Create an S3 bucket with a specified name
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "my_s3_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-unique-bucket-name"  # Ensure the bucket name is globally unique
  acl    = "private"               # Set the ACL to private
}

# Configure ownership controls for the S3 bucket
resource "aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" "my_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.my_s3_bucket.id  # Reference the bucket ID

  rule {
    object_ownership = "BucketOwnerPreferred"  # Set object ownership to BucketOwnerPreferred
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region. You can change this to any other valid AWS region as needed.
2. **S3 Bucket Creation**: An S3 bucket named `my-unique-bucket-name` is created. Ensure that the bucket name is globally unique across all existing bucket names in Amazon S3.
3. **Ownership Controls**: The `aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls` resource is configured to reference the S3 bucket created earlier. The ownership rule is set to `BucketOwnerPreferred`, ensuring that the bucket owner automatically owns and has full control over every object in the bucket.

