The Terraform program defines a DynamoDB table named "GameScores" with a billing mode set to "PAY_PER_REQUEST". It includes the necessary attributes and keys as specified. Additionally, it configures the on-demand throughput settings with a maximum of 1000 read and write request units. The program also ensures that all attributes are indexed by removing the unused attribute "TopScore".

### Terraform HCL Program
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "dynamodb_table" {
  name           = "GameScores"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key       = "UserId"
  range_key      = "GameTitle"

  attribute {
    name = "UserId"
    type = "S"
  }

  attribute {
    name = "GameTitle"
    type = "S"
  }

  on_demand_throughput {
    max_read_request_units  = 1000
    max_write_request_units = 1000
  }

  tags = {
    Name        = "dynamodb-table-1"
    Environment = "production"
  }
}
```

This configuration ensures that the DynamoDB table is created with the specified attributes and keys, and the on-demand throughput settings are configured correctly. The unused attribute "TopScore" has been removed to satisfy the requirement that all attributes must be indexed.

