The Terraform program provided fetches the latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI from the specified region and creates a copy of it in the same region. The program uses the `aws_ami` data source to find the latest AMI and then creates a new AMI using the `aws_ami` resource. The program includes a provider configuration for AWS and a variable for specifying the source AMI region.

### Terraform HCL Program
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

data "aws_ami" "latest_amazon_linux_2_ami" {
  most_recent = true

  filter {
    name   = "name"
