### Description

This Terraform program creates an S3 Glacier vault and applies a Vault Lock to it. The Vault Lock enforces compliance and immutability by setting rules such as the default retrieval bypass, maximum retrieval bytes per second, and minimum days to retain an unlocked vault. The program uses the AWS provider and specifies the region and vault name as variables with default values.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = var.region
}

variable "region" {
  description = "The AWS region to deploy the resources"
  default     = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_glacier_vault" "s3_glacier_vault" {
  name = var.vault_name
}

resource "aws_glacier_vault_lock" "s3_glacier_vault_lock" {
  complete_lock = true
  policy        = jsonencode({
    Rules = [{
      DefaultRetrievalBypass = false
      MaximumRetrievalBytesPerSecond = 1048576
      MinDaysToRetainUnlockedVault = 30
    }]
  })
  vault_name    = aws_glacier_vault.s3_glacier_vault.name
}

variable "vault_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 Glacier vault"
  default     = "my-glacier-vault"
}
```

This configuration ensures that the S3 Glacier vault is created first, and then the Vault Lock is applied to it. The Vault Lock policy is defined using a JSON-encoded policy document that specifies the rules for retrieval and retention.

