### Description
This Terraform configuration creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with a listener that has a fixed-response action. The fixed-response action returns a simple HTTP response to any incoming requests. The configuration also includes an IAM role and policy to ensure the load balancer has the necessary permissions.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "example_load_balancer" {
  name               = "example-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  subnets            = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]
  security_groups    = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]

  tags = {
    Name = "example-alb"
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "example_listener" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.example_load_balancer.arn
  port              = "80"
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type = "fixed-response"

    fixed_response {
      content_type = "text/plain"
      message_body = "Fixed response content"
      status_code  = "200"
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "example_iam_role" {
  name = "example-iam-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "elasticloadbalancing.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "example_iam_policy" {
  name        = "example-iam-policy"
  description = "Policy for ELB"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "ec2:Describe*",
          "elasticloadbalancing:*"
        ]
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "example_role_policy_attachment" {
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.example_iam_policy.arn
  role       = aws_iam_role.example_iam_role.name
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **Load Balancer (ALB)**: An Application Load Balancer is created with two subnets and a security group. The `subnets` and `security_groups` values are placeholders and should be replaced with actual subnet and security group IDs.
3. **Listener**: A listener is attached to the load balancer on port 80 with the HTTP protocol. The listener has a default action that returns a fixed response with a status code of 200 and a message body of "Fixed response content".
4. **IAM Role and Policy**: An IAM role and policy are created to grant the load balancer necessary permissions. The role trusts the Elastic Load Balancing service, and the policy allows EC2 and Elastic Load Balancing actions on all resources.

